<title>USA: Armenia seeks 21,000 T optional origin wheat-agent.</title>
<headline>Armenia seeks 21,000 T optional origin wheat-agent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Armenia will be seeking 21,000 tonnes optional origin wheat for up to November 20 shipment, its U.S. export agent said.</p>
<p>The wheat would come from the European Community, Ukraine or if U.S. origin, only hard red winter no.2.</p>
<p>Wheat characteristics in the commercial tender included 14 percent maximum moisture content and four percent maximum broken kernels.</p>
<p>The latest date for offers was October 14, in Yerevan, Armenia.</p>
<p>--Doris Frankel 312-983-7305</p>
</text>
